fi
sound PO5.aac
text @[Akio]
text Everything is fine. Calm down, stupid.
text The doctor has just finished his examination.
setvar strS[1001] = "NONE"
setvar intF[1113] = intF[1112]
bgload {$strS[1000]}.jpg 30
if intF[1113] == 1
	if strS[1000] < "C"
		setimg {$strS[1004]}.png -7 -7
	fi
fi
sound PO6.aac
text @[Doctor]
text It's the same as with Nagisa-san.
text He makes the announcement to us.
text Which means it's not a cold, but a fever brought on by unknown causes...
text ...And that she has an illness that will follow her for the rest of her life.
text @[Tomoya]
text She was so lively until just yesterday...
text @[Tomoya]
text She was always so full of energy...
text I sit down on the ground.
sound PO7.aac
text @[Doctor]
text Now if you'll excuse me.
text The doctor leaves the room.
sound PO8.aac
text @[Sanae]
text Thank you very much.
text I see Sanae-san's legs pass in front of me as she goes to see the doctor off.
text ...It's all so similar to back then.
text Is this... fate?
text Are we stuck in the flow of time, helpless and at the constant mercy of the whims of unknown forces...?
text Are all of our efforts meaningless?
text In the end... do all of our actions go unrewarded?
sound PO9.aac
text @[Akio]
text Hey, Tomoya.
text I hear the old man's voice.
text He must be right behind me. I stay there with my eyes to the floor.
sound POA.aac
text @[Akio]
text Remind me who her father is again.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text @[Tomoya]
text ...Me.
sound POB.aac
text @[Akio]
text Then get a hold of yourself.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text I raise my head.
text And I take a look at reality.
text Will I be able to live... as the fathers I've known lived?
text The old man is a strong person.
text I'm not the only one who lost Nagisa.
text My old man was an impressive father too.
text He sacrificed everything to raise me.
text Will I be able to become a parent who's as strong as them...?
text ......
text Ushio's eyes are looking at me.
text Not Sanae-san, not the old man. Me.
text That's right.
text I don't have a choice. That's the kind of parent I have to be.
text I've been living my life since that day so that I can.
