text I clean up my belongings in the evening.
text My diagonal pliers, with their worn-in grip.
text My knife with one-centimeter markings. I've had it sharpened so many times that it's strikingly smaller than when I first got it.
text The towel I got from Johnny-san, now thin after so many wash cycles.
text And finally, the tool bag and marked-up screwdriver set I got from Yoshino-san.
text I place my well-used tools into the bag, leaving behind nothing but a clothes hanger.
text Before me is a completely empty locker.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...This thing was pretty big.
text The locker had started to feel cramped at some point because of all the stuff in it.
text I'd stopped even noticing, but it makes me feel the reality of just how long I've been here.
